{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794050397,"nonce":"iGF+fXBu7KS/Y/KE4rkC53ucDnY=","title":"Binary secret values are converted to text lossily","message":"`resolve_step_secrets` reads secret values with `from_utf8_lossy`, so a value that is not UTF-8 reaches the Step changed, and the redactor registers the changed text. This was true before secrets became files (bcf2c11). Files can now carry bytes.\n\nFix: make `ResolvedSecrets` hold `Vec\u003cu8\u003e`, write bytes to the per-Pod Secret's `data` and the local files, and refuse a non-UTF-8 value for `env: true`.\n\nEvidence: review X2 / C2-4 in ~/.afk/scrarab-ci/20261107-0247-decisions/review/safety.md.","files":null}]}